===Etymology===
{{root|en|ine-pro|*bʰeyd-}}
From {{inh|en|enm|bot}}, {{m|enm|boot}}, {{m|enm|boet}}, {{m|enm|boyt|t=boat}}, from {{inh|en|ang|bāt|t=boat}}, from {{inh|en|gmw-pro|*bait}}, from {{inh|en|gem-pro|*baitaz}}, {{m|gem-pro|*baitą|t=boat, small ship}}, from {{der|en|ine-pro|*bʰeyd-|t=to break, split}}. Cognate with {{cog|non|beit|t=boat}}, {{cog|dum|beitel|t=little boat}}.

{{cog|non|bátr}} (whence {{cog|is|bátur}}, {{cog|no|båt}}, {{cog|da|båd}}), {{cog|nl|boot}}, {{cog|de|Boot}}, {{cog|oc|batèl}} and {{cog|fr|bateau}} are all ultimately borrowings from the Old English word.

